WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.286
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.286 --> 00:00:15.020
Triggers, part two: who a trigger hits, when it runs, and how triggers remember things.

5
00:00:16.433 --> 00:00:20.581
Open Mechanics, then Advanced, then Triggers, and open bramble swipe.

6
00:00:20.581 --> 00:00:21.963
Scope is set to player.

7
00:00:21.963 --> 00:00:24.367
Normally a trigger hits the whole party,

8
00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:27.974
but with player scope it lands on the player who set it off.

9
00:00:28.433 --> 00:00:33.390
Its condition is an action check: the AI reads what the player is trying to do,

10
00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.272
before the story gets written.

11
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:40.242
The effect takes five health, with the target set to satisfying players,

12
00:00:40.242 --> 00:00:42.558
so only the one who did it gets hurt.

13
00:00:42.558 --> 00:00:46.565
Studio shows an empty target as all players, so set it yourself.

14
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:52.492
And this story note lands in this turn's narration: Bramble swats them flat.

15
00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:54.717
That's because of the phase.

16
00:00:54.717 --> 00:01:00.831
A trigger with an action check runs in planning, before the story, so its notes reach this turn.

17
00:01:00.831 --> 00:01:06.117
Everything else runs in the state phase, after the story, and shapes the next turn.

18
00:01:06.117 --> 00:01:11.022
You rarely need this box: only to pin a fully mechanical trigger to planning.

19
00:01:12.433 --> 00:01:16.606
Now flags. Back in the triggers list, open met Lucius.

20
00:01:16.606 --> 00:01:20.161
It fires once, when the story has Lucius Gilt,

21
00:01:20.161 --> 00:01:24.334
the rival ringmaster, meeting the player face to face.

22
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.701
Its only effect writes a flag, met lucius, set to true.

23
00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:31.963
A flag is just something your world remembers.

24
00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.215
Gilt watching reads that flag.

25
00:01:34.215 --> 00:01:39.598
Once it's true and the party's back at camp, one of Gilt's big men turns up at the hedge.

26
00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:45.119
Both of its checks are mechanical, so it never spends one of the turn's limited story checks.

27
00:01:45.119 --> 00:01:49.658
Judge something once, save it as a flag, and let every other trigger read the flag.

28
00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:55.335
One catch: read a flag back as the same type you wrote it.

29
00:01:55.335 --> 00:01:59.530
A true or false read as a number just comes back as zero.

30
00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:02.375
That's triggers 102.

31
00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:04.899
Ours are linked in the description.

32
00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:09.873
Next time, scripts: a little code that does the work of ten triggers.

33
00:02:10.333 --> 00:02:14.281
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

